{title: What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{artist: Joseph M. Scriven}
{key: G}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune CONVERSE - Charles C. Converse (1868)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1855, tune 1868: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]What a friend we [C]have in [G]Jesus, all our sins and [D]griefs to [G]bear!
[G]What a privi[C]lege to [G]carry everything to [D]God in [G]prayer!
[D]O what peace we [G]often forfeit, [D]O what needless [G]pain we [D]bear,
[G]All because we [C]do not [G]carry everything to [D]God in [G]prayer!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Have we trials [C]and temp[G]tations? Is there trouble [D]any[G]where?
[G]We should never [C]be dis[G]couraged; take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
[D]Can we find a [G]friend so faithful [D]who will all our [G]sorrows [D]share?
[G]Jesus knows our [C]every [G]weakness; take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Are we weak and [C]heavy-[G]laden, cumbered with a [D]load of [G]care?
[G]Precious Savior, [C]still our [G]refuge; take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
[D]Do thy friends de[G]spise, forsake thee? [D]Take it to the [G]Lord in [D]prayer!
[G]In His arms He'll [C]take and [G]shield thee; thou wilt find a [D]solace [G]there.
{end_of_verse}
